                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/AppHeader/AppHeader.vue",
                    "line": 49,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Language selector removed from navbar entirely per #50. Remaining navbar items (Health, Power, Refresh, user dropdown) are standard b-nav-item/b-button/b-dropdown elements."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/AppHeader/AppHeader.vue",
                    "line": 50,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "navbar is getting too busy.  I would argue that this is an item that users would use only once, if ever.  Move it to the `app-header-user` dropdown as it is a better fit."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/AppHeader/AppHeader.vue",
                    "line": 50,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Language selector moved inside app-header-user dropdown between Profile settings and Log out, with <b-dropdown-divider> separators and auto-close=\"outside\" so users can interact with the select without the dropdown closing."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/AppHeader/AppHeader.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sivaprabu Ganesan",
                        "email": "sivaprabug@ami.com",
                        "username": "sivaprabug"
                    },
                    "message": "data-test-id=\"login-select-language\" used on the AppHeader language selector"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/AppHeader/AppHeader.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Changed data-test-id=\"login-select-language\" to data-test-id=\"app-header-select-language\" since the selector is now in the app header user dropdown, not the login page."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/AppHeader/AppHeader.vue",
                    "line": 153,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sivaprabu Ganesan",
                        "email": "sivaprabug@ami.com",
                        "username": "sivaprabug"
                    },
                    "message": "The same languages array already exists in src/views/Login/Login.vue. This is a direct duplication. When a new locale is added to src/locales/, it must be added in three places: the locale file, Login.vue, and now AppHeader.vue. This will inevitably fall out of sync."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/AppHeader/AppHeader.vue",
                    "line": 153,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Agreed.  This is a sin of Login.vue that I should have addressed when we added vendor language override support to i18n.js.\n\nThis should be something like:\n```\nconst languages = computed(() => getAvailableLanguages(availableLocales));\n```\n\nand then in i18n.js:\n```\n// Build a {value, text} list for a language picker from a set of locale codes.\n// Drops bare-language aliases (those without a region suffix) so each language\n// only appears once, and resolves the native display name via Intl.DisplayNames.\nexport function getAvailableLanguages(locales) {\n  return (locales || [])\n    .filter((loc) => loc.includes('-'))\n    .map((loc) => {\n      const language = new Intl.Locale(loc).language;\n      let name;\n      try {\n        name = new Intl.DisplayNames([loc], { type: 'language' }).of(language);\n      } catch {\n        name = loc;\n      }\n      const text = name\n        ? name.charAt(0).toLocaleUpperCase(loc) + name.slice(1)\n        : loc;\n      return { value: loc, text };\n    })\n    .sort((a, b) => a.value.localeCompare(b.value));\n}\n```\n\nHere I used Intl.DisplayNames, otherwise every strings file would need a special key for its Display name."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/AppHeader/AppHeader.vue",
                    "line": 153,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Implemented exactly as suggested: getAvailableLanguages(locales) exported from i18n.js using Intl.DisplayNames. Both AppHeader and Login use computed(() => getAvailableLanguages(availableLocales)). No hardcoded language arrays remain. Label format is \"{English name} - {Native name}\" (e.g., \"Russian - \u0420\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0439\", \"US - English\")."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/AppHeader/AppHeader.vue",
                    "line": 228,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "probably out of scope for a component.  Instead just call global/setLanguagePreference from here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/AppHeader/AppHeader.vue",
                    "line": 228,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Removed the computed setter. currentLocale is now a plain getter. languageChange(locale) handles setting $i18n.locale and committing to global/setLanguagePreference. The $i18n.locale assignment remains in the component as it's required for Vue i18n reactivity \u2014 the store mutation handles persistence only."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/AppHeader/AppHeader.vue",
                    "line": 284,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "don't need this.  add the localStorage set to the global/setLanguagePreference function.  And you could emit the language-change event from there too.\n\nLogin.vue should be updated to match."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/AppHeader/AppHeader.vue",
                    "line": 284,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. localStorage.setItem('storedLanguage', ...) moved exclusively into the setLanguagePreference mutation in GlobalStore.js. All direct localStorage calls removed from AppHeader.vue and Login.vue (both the watch handler and login() method). The mutation now owns both state update and persistence."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/Global/PageTitle.vue",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sivaprabu Ganesan",
                        "email": "sivaprabug@ami.com",
                        "username": "sivaprabug"
                    },
                    "message": "logic duplicated across App.vue and PageTitle.vue"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/components/Global/PageTitle.vue",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Route-title derivation logic extracted to getRoutePageTitle(route, t, te, fallback) in i18n.js. Both App.vue (updateDocumentTitle) and PageTitle.vue (title computed) now call this shared function."
                }
